LAST_SUCCESS=Task 117 M2 step 2b DONE — H.264 wired into the host + real MP4 plays end-to-end. Host: video::Codec::H264 + video/avc mime, codec2b/codec_of map it, desktop enables openh264 feature (lights up H.264 on BOTH desktop-openh264 AND Android-MediaCodec-HW). h264_mp4toannexb implemented (~40 lines). Present queue is now a REORDER BUFFER (PTS-order insert) for B-frames. --video-decode-file <mp4> plays a real file through the host VideoDecoder: bbb-h264.mp4 (1280x720, real B-frames) = 300/300 decoded+presented, 0 dropped, order OK, drift avg 0.8ms, snapshot = correct decoded frame. Host desktop + Android cross-build green.
NOTES=REAL BUG FIXED: openh264 default flush-after-every-decode overflows the reorder buffer at 2nd GOP (lost 236/300, returning success per frame) — backend now opens Flush::NoFlush + flush_remaining at EOS. The in-crate no-B-frame round-trip never hit it: real files are a different test. repros/h264-mp4-decode proves 300/300. Reorder is host-adapter policy (a call never reorders), not codec. mp4 crate is a diagnostic-only desktop dep (prod demux is guest-side). NEXT: HW backends — VAAPI on popos (real /dev/dri + iHD driver, has H264 VLD); then H.265 (HW-only desktop). The --video-decode-file harness + reorder buffer are reusable for the rest of the source×backend matrix. Android H.264 HW path wired (video/avc) but NOT yet device-tested.
